    bool "NS16550 I/O-port UART backend (early console)"
    depends on KFEAT_CHAR && ARCH_X86_64
    default y if MACHINE_X86_64_QEMU
    help
      Build the NS16550 I/O-port UART backend used by the early-boot console
      and the per-instance serial driver.

    bool "PL011 per-instance serial driver"
    depends on KFEAT_CHAR && ARCH_AARCH64
    select KFEAT_DRIVER_CONSOLE_PL011
    default y if MACHINE_AARCH64_QEMU
    help
      Enable the kdriver per-instance serial driver for PL011 UARTs. Each UART
      node becomes a character device; the stdout UART shares the early-boot
      instance.

    bool "virtio-blk driver on the driver-core model (PCI)"
    default n
    help
      Enable the new-model virtio-blk driver registered in the driver-core
      device domain: const PCI id table, guards-in-Data activation (no
      global side tables), and block-class publication through a detached
      class parent. This is the migration target for
      KFEAT_DRIVER_VIRTIO_BLK; enable it instead of (not in addition to)
      the legacy symbol.

    bool "virtio-net driver on the driver-core model (PCI)"
    default n
    help
      Enable the new-model virtio-net driver: const PCI id table, per-device
      interrupt ownership (no global IRQ routing), and net-class publication
      through a detached class parent. Migration target for
      KFEAT_DRIVER_VIRTIO_NET; enable it instead of the legacy symbol.

    bool "virtio-rng driver on the driver-core model (PCI)"
    default n
    help
      Enable the new-model virtio-rng driver: const PCI id table and char
      class publication through a detached parent. Migration target for
      KFEAT_DRIVER_VIRTIO_RNG.

    bool "ramdisk driver on the driver-core model"
    default n
    help
      Enable the new-model ramdisk driver: alias-matched board-static device
      publishing a block disk. Migration target for KFEAT_DRIVER_RAMDISK.

    bool "virtio-gpu driver on the driver-core model (PCI)"
    default n
    help

